[task/give-first-calcs-2026-09-04 9256633] fix: remove implied industry benchmarks from calculator defaults
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

Committed as `9256633`.

**What changed:**

**SeasonalCapacityCalculator.tsx** — `DEFAULT_DEMAND_PCT` (`[60, 55, 70, 85, 100, 110, 115, 90, 105, 100, 80, 65]`) removed entirely. Replaced with `FLAT_DEMAND_PCT` (`Array(12).fill(100)`) — every month starts at 100%, a neutral flat line with no implied seasonal pattern. "Reset to default" button renamed to "Reset to flat". Baseline hint updated to explain the flat starting state.

**CapacityPlannerCalculator.tsx** — Removed "10–20% is typical" from the downtime hint (`CapacityPlannerCalculator.tsx:110`). The default value of 15 stays as a neutral starting point; the text no longer frames it as an industry norm. No other benchmark-flavoured defaults found — the remaining defaults (4 machines, 8 hours, 5 days, 30 min/job) are neutral operational inputs, not claimed industry figures.
